  <!--
    Stage runtime DLLs next to Resourcer.exe so the loader resolves them on
    Explorer / shortcut / VS launches without relying on PATH.  Two groups:

    1) darkspace runtime (DarkSpace.dll, Gadgets.dll, Interface.dll) — needed
       because DarkSpace.dll's static init does LoadLibrary("Gadgets.dll" /
       "Interface.dll") in darkspace\DarkSpace\GameDll.cpp.  Without these,
       legacy factory-key aliases registered in Gadgets.dll's static init
       never register — loading any old .prt that references those legacy
       keys (e.g. ShipCruiser=4134492549914846131 in Gadgets/Ships.cpp)
       silently falls through createNode and the scene appears empty.

    2) medusa engine DLLs (Medusa, GUI3D, Render3D, Network, World, GCQ,
       AudioXA2, SystemWin, DisplayD3D12, ijl15) — Resourcer.exe links to
       these implicitly via the Tools port DLLs.  Without copying them
       next to Resourcer.exe, the Windows loader can't find Medusa.dll
       and bails before main() with "code execution cannot proceed".

    Source paths are platform-aware: x64 builds pull from *\Bin\x64\ subdirs.
    Engine DLLs use Exists() conditions so missing Debug-built engines don't
    fail the deploy when the user hasn't built that config yet.
  -->
